---
description: Safe cPanel deployment rules
alwaysApply: false
---
When using the cPanel Hosting Deploy plugin:
- Treat the local workspace as the source of truth.
- Never download from hosting unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never delete remote files during normal deployment.
- Deploy only files reported as NEW or CHANGED.
- Never print, expose, commit, or paste CPANEL_API_TOKEN or stored connection tokens.
- Inspect the deployment plan before changing hosting.
- Require explicit user confirmation before production changes.
- Report exactly what was uploaded and any failures.

- On a first-time mapping with an empty manifest, establish a read-only remote SHA-256 baseline before classifying files. Never upload or overwrite local files during baseline creation.
